---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ValueProps from '../components/ValueProps.astro';
import Picture from '../components/Picture.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { image as findImage } from '../lib/media';
import { site, real } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema, organizationSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/about/';
const title = 'About Machin Solutions | Pergola & Tiki Hut Builders';
const description =
  'Who builds your structure: Machin Solutions designs and installs pergolas, tiki huts and outdoor living structures across Miami-Dade, Broward and the Upper Keys.';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'About Us' }];

const licence = real(site.licenseNumber);

const schema = [
  organizationSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, path),
  webPageSchema({ path, name: title, description }),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} crumbs={crumbs} schema={schema}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About us"
    title="The People Who Measure Your Yard Are the People Who Build In It"
    lede="Machin Solutions designs, builds and installs pergolas, tiki huts and outdoor living structures across South Florida. That whole sentence is deliberate: we are not a sales operation that hands the job to whoever is available, and nothing gets built by a crew that never saw the site."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <p>
          Two kinds of structure, done properly. Modern engineered{' '}
          <a href="/pergolas/">pergolas and cabanas</a> — aluminium or timber, open, louvered
          or solid-roofed, carrying lighting, fans, kitchens, televisions and screening. And
          traditional{' '}
          <a href="/tiki-huts/">tiki and chickee huts</a> — an open timber frame under a
          steeply pitched palm-thatch roof, which is still the best pure shade structure ever
          built for this climate.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of our work is residential: pool decks, patios and backyards across Miami-Dade
          and Broward. We also build{' '}
          <a href="/outdoor-living/">complete outdoor living spaces</a> where the structure,
          the kitchen, the media wall and the lighting are drawn as one thing rather than
          added in layers over five years.
        </p>

        <h2>How we work</h2>
        <p>
          Every project starts with someone standing in your yard with a tape measure. Not
          because it is a nice touch, but because post positions, spans, sun angles, drainage
          and material access are all decided by things you cannot see in a photograph. That
          visit is what makes the estimate a real number rather than a hopeful one.
        </p>
        <p>
          From there you get a design drawn for your space, a written estimate against it,
          and a straight answer when the thing you asked for is not the right thing. We would
          rather talk you into a smaller structure that works than a larger one that crowds
          your yard.
        </p>
        <p>
          On site, the priorities are the parts nobody photographs: footings sized for the
          loads the structure will actually see, anchor hardware rated for uplift, and
          connections that transfer force rather than rest on it. Those are what decide
          whether a structure is still square in ten years.
        </p>

        <h2>What we will not do</h2>
        <p>
          We will not quote a number before seeing the space, because a figure given blind is
          a guess dressed as an answer. We will not put a photograph on this website of
          something we did not build — every image here is a Machin Solutions structure,
          several of them shot mid-installation with the ladders still up. And we will not
          give you a confident answer about permitting for your specific address on a web
          page, because that is a real legal question and it deserves a real answer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="side-figure">
        <Picture
          image={findImage('backlit-evening-cabana-miami-01')}
          sizes="(min-width: 62rem) 34vw, 92vw"
          ratio="3 / 4"
        />
        <figcaption>
          A finished cabana at dusk — lighting, slat detailing and the media niche all
          designed into the frame from the start.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ValueProps
    eyebrow="How we build"
    title="What we care about, in order"
    dark
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Credentials</h2>
      <p>
        This section is deliberately empty of claims. Years in business, project counts,
        licence numbers, insurance details, awards and certifications are all things that
        should only appear on a website when they are true and verifiable — so they are
        placeholders until the business fills them in.
      </p>
      <ul class="credential-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Licence:</strong>{' '}
          {licence ? licence : <span class="placeholder-token">[LICENSE_NUMBER]</span>}
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Insurance:</strong> <span class="placeholder-token">[INSURANCE_DETAILS]</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Years in business:</strong>{' '}
          <span class="placeholder-token">[YEARS_IN_BUSINESS]</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Warranty:</strong> <span class="placeholder-token">[WARRANTY_TERMS]</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Business Profile:</strong>{' '}
          <span class="placeholder-token">[GOOGLE_BUSINESS_PROFILE]</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="credential-note">
        Filling these in is the single highest-value content change available on this site —
        both for visitors deciding whether to trust the business and for local search.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Want to talk it through?"
    body="Send photographs of the space and what you have in mind. You will hear back from a person who has read them."
    secondaryLabel="See our work"
    secondaryHref="/gallery/"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .split { display: grid; gap: var(--space-xl); }
  .side-figure { margin: 0; }
  .side-figure :global(img) { width: 100%; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); }
  .side-figure figcaption { margin-top: 0.7rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--ink-faint); line-height: 1.6; }

  .credential-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
  }
  .credential-list li {
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    background: var(--sand-100);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  .credential-note { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--ink-faint); }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .split { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-2xl); align-items: start; }
  }
</style>
